She testified that the Medical Board

examined the deceased on 7 November 2004 and made the following findings:
a. The deceased had sustained burns in her pubic region, breasts, and the

 frontal area of her scalp;
b. No foreign hair was found in the pubic region of the deceased;

 c. A pathological report based on a vaginal smear revealed that there was

 no spermatozoa (living or dead) in the pubic region of the deceased;

PART A

 d. A vaginal examination revealed that two fingers were admitted easily;

 and

 e. The deceased had 14 upper and lower teeth, which were incomplete. The pubic symphysis was 40%. An X-ray of her wrist indicated that she

 was below 17 years.
